  "rationale": "Both answers are valid for the physical sense of “shallow,” but the national split is materially overstated if “different-common-word” implies exclusivity. Indonesian dangkal is the stronger general answer, while cetek is also an accepted Indonesian form marked as Jakarta Malay; Malaysian Malay dictionaries explicitly define both cetek and dangkal as synonyms. The answers need not change, but the relation should reflect preferred overlap rather than a clean national divide. No false-friend contrast is supported or required.",
