      "subject": "English cue and sense",
      "conclusion": "Correct: “shallow” can mean having a short distance from top to bottom, matching “not deep.”",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/dictionary/english/shallow"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Indonesian answer: dangkal",
      "conclusion": "Correct and appropriate as the stronger general Indonesian answer for the physical sense.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://kbbi.web.id/dangkal.html"
      ],
      "evidence_limitation": "The dictionary establishes meaning and acceptance, but not comparative national frequency."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Indonesian overlap: cetek",
      "conclusion": "Cetek is also an accepted Indonesian equivalent, although the KBBI entry marks it as Jakarta Malay; therefore it is not a strictly Malaysian-only form.",
      "material_risk": true,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://kbbi.web.id/cetek"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Malaysian Malay answer: cetek",
      "conclusion": "Correct and standard for Malaysian Malay; DBP defines it as “tidak dalam” and explicitly gives dangkal as an equivalent.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=73980&keyword=cetek"
      ]
